## Authentication

| Transport | Mechanisms |
| --- | --- |
| `winrm` | `basic`, `ntlm`, `kerberos` |
| `ssh` | password, private key |

WinRM `basic` authentication only accepts local accounts, so it cannot be used with a
domain account on a domain controller. `ntlm` over plain HTTP requires
`AllowUnencrypted = true` on the WinRM service, because NTLM message encryption is not
applied; prefer HTTPS on port 5986. `kerberos` requires the target's FQDN rather than
an IP address, since the SPN is derived from the host name.

